{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And this is what you shall do, etc.</b> The meaning of the matter is that the sons of Kohath should not be left to their own discretion to carry as they wish, for then, given the beloved nature of the sacred service, everyone would rush to serve and they would end up inadvertently transgressing. Rather, Aaron and his sons shall assign them, each man, etc., and in this way each one recognizes his place. This is what it means by <b>and they shall assign them, each man</b>, etc. And this is what it means by <b>and they shall not come to see</b> — meaning, so that they do not come to a state of seeing at the moment the sacred objects are swallowed [i.e., covered]. And the meaning of <b>and they shall assign</b> is that merely each one recognizing his place alone does not suffice, but rather he may not enter and put his hand to carry until Aaron and his sons say to him: So-and-so, put your hand in such-and-such a place to carry — and so on in this manner. This is what it means by <b>and they shall assign them</b>. And therefore you will find in the command regarding the sons of Gershon that although Scripture says ״עַל פִּי אַהֲרֹן וּבָנָיו תִּהְיֶה כָּל עֲבוֹדַת״ etc. (Numbers 4:27), it does not say ״וְשָׂמוּ״ etc." "<b>And they shall live and not die.</b> Meaning, for by their involvement with the Ark, which contains the Torah — which is the source of life — they will lengthen their days. And out of concern for the harm that could come from touching and seeing it, He said <b>and they shall not die</b>:" "<b>Thus concludes the parashah of Numbers.</b>"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:03.491003230Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}